import{_ as i,o as t,c as n,a2 as a}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const p=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 902 | Myriad-Rank Republican Civilizational Charter · Article 1 — Enshrining Anti-Predationism in the Constitution","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 902 | Myriad-Rank Republican Civilizational Charter · Article 1 — Enshrining Anti-Predationism in the Constitution","no":902,"module":5,"tags":["Charter","Article 1","Anti-Predation","Constitutional Enshrinement","Fundamental Clause"],"related":["04-Anti-Predationism Core Thesis","47-Anti-Monopoly Law","19-Cultivation Ethics and Boundaries"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0902_模块5-第一条-反掠夺主义入宪.md","filePath":"en/0902_模块5-第一条-反掠夺主义入宪.md"}'),o={name:"en/0902_模块5-第一条-反掠夺主义入宪.md"};function r(s,e,l,c,h,d){return t(),n("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[a('<h1 id="entry-902-myriad-rank-republican-civilizational-charter-·-article-1-—-enshrining-anti-predationism-in-the-constitution" tabindex="-1">Entry 902 | Myriad-Rank Republican Civilizational Charter · Article 1 — Enshrining Anti-Predationism in the Constitution <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-902-myriad-rank-republican-civilizational-charter-·-article-1-—-enshrining-anti-predationism-in-the-constitution" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 902 | Myriad-Rank Republican Civilizational Charter · Article 1 — Enshrining Anti-Predationism in the Constitution&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 5 · Civilization Final-Finalization Canonical Entries | Benchmark base: Documents 04, 47, 19</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-write-do-not-predate-into-civilization-s-first-article" tabindex="-1">Introduction: write &quot;do not predate&quot; into civilization&#39;s first article <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-write-do-not-predate-into-civilization-s-first-article" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: write &quot;do not predate&quot; into civilization&#39;s first article&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The reason the charter&#39;s first article is enshrining anti-predationism is that before all institutional design, one must first answer what civilization stands on. Among the six top-level axioms, the anti-predation axiom holds the first place — develop increments, do not consume stock; do not use slaughter and predation as the evolutionary path; the Great Dao is fully open at all levels, no private hoarding, no monopoly. Placing this article first means all other charter articles are its unfolding and guarantee: Myriad-Rank republicanism is anti-predation&#39;s unfolding at the subject layer; collective ascension is anti-predation&#39;s unfolding at the direction layer; causal self-discipline is anti-predation&#39;s unfolding at the boundary layer; the law-first axiom is anti-predation&#39;s unfolding at the stability layer. Article 1&#39;s enshrinement equals declaring: the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization from birth draws a line with the predatory system.</p><p>Together with the previous five axioms, this article is also bound by Axiom 6 · Universal Equal Infinite Law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing and layabouts retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will not be eliminated by the times; strivers and Youth Supremes may superimpose more and higher levels of infinity; predation thus fundamentally loses meaning.</p><h2 id="i-jurisprudential-basis" tabindex="-1">I. Jurisprudential Basis <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-jurisprudential-basis" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. Jurisprudential Basis&quot;">​</a></h2><p>This article&#39;s jurisprudential basis directly comes from the Anti-Predationism Core Thesis (Document 04)&#39;s triple-fallacy argument: predationism misjudges the cosmos as a finite hunting ground (cosmology fallacy), places the strong&#39;s evolutionary right above the weak&#39;s right to life (ethics fallacy), mistakes predation as the most efficient path (efficiency fallacy). The thesis already proves predatory cultivation has four ceilings — impure origin, refining consumes spirit, resistance cost, ability degradation; the higher one goes, the more impassable. Therefore declaring predation illegal is not moral high-talk, but a legislative choice based on objective cosmic laws — in Heng Yuan Zhou predation is &quot;this road does not go&quot;; constitutional enshrinement only writes this objective fact down.</p><h2 id="ii-normative-content-six-prohibited-predation-forms" tabindex="-1">II. Normative Content: Six Prohibited Predation Forms <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-normative-content-six-prohibited-predation-forms" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Normative Content: Six Prohibited Predation Forms&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Article 1 uses enumeration plus catch-all to constitutionally prohibit all the following forms:</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Form</th><th>Constitutional Prohibition</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Energy predation</td><td>Directly devouring others&#39; cultivation energy and origin</td></tr><tr><td>Fortune predation</td><td>Secret arts stealing clan or individual fortune</td></tr><tr><td>Dharma-door monopoly</td><td>Using transmission authorization in exchange for loyalty, monopolizing the Great Dao</td></tr><tr><td>Plane colonization</td><td>Conquering low-tier planes to predate resources and population</td></tr><tr><td>Spiritual enslavement</td><td>Soul control, turning beings into cultivation tools</td></tr><tr><td>Resource draining</td><td>Unrestricted extraction, causing plane-membrane collapse</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Any cultivation system taking predation as its core is uniformly declared illegal; there is no excuse space for &quot;gray predation,&quot; &quot;limited predation,&quot; or &quot;just predation.&quot;</p><h2 id="iii-scope" tabindex="-1">III. Scope <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-scope" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Scope&quot;">​</a></h2><p>This article applies to all individuals, clans, sects, and civilizational institutions, regardless of realm. Origin Realm, plane-sovereign strong ones, and Sense-Realm new cultivators are equally bound by this article; the higher the realm, the heavier the violation consequence — because the strong one&#39;s predation exponentially amplifies damage to the network. This article also applies to cross-plane and cross-time operations: predating in other planes or historical periods is as guilty as predating in the home plane at present.</p><h2 id="iv-consequences-of-violation" tabindex="-1">IV. Consequences of Violation <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-consequences-of-violation" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Consequences of Violation&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Violating Article 1 is one of the charter&#39;s most serious unconstitutionality types. The consequence ladder is: all predated gains uniformly recovered; origin forcibly purified and residual traces of others&#39; will removed; predatory cultivators stripped of corresponding realm qualification, transferred to ethics-transformation procedure; those causing the predated&#39;s death or plane-membrane damage, the Symbiotic Court per anti-predation clauses imposes life-long limits on their anchor access; those styling themselves &quot;enlightened predators&quot; or &quot;justified rascals,&quot; using clever means to circumvent enumerated clauses, are pursued under the catch-all clause; no exemption because means are covert.</p><h2 id="v-supervision-mechanism" tabindex="-1">V. Supervision Mechanism <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-supervision-mechanism" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Supervision Mechanism&quot;">​</a></h2><p>This article is executed throughout by Alaya Network + multi-layer supervision: the anchor network automatically compares energy sources; any foreign energy carrying the original owner&#39;s residual will immediately triggers an alert; the Myriad-Rank-republican council&#39;s anti-predation committee under it is dedicated to investigation; the Symbiotic Court sets a predation-cases dedicated tribunal; each clan retains direct-report and constitutional-suit rights. Supervision does not rely on the parties&#39; voluntary surrender, but network real-time causal monitoring — in Heng Yuan Zhou predation is almost impossible to leave no traces; this is precisely the technical basis for anti-predation&#39;s constitutional enshrinement truly landing.</p><h2 id="vi-after-constitutional-enshrinement-from-prohibition-to-culture" tabindex="-1">VI. After Constitutional Enshrinement: From Prohibition to Culture <a class="header-anchor" href="#vi-after-constitutional-enshrinement-from-prohibition-to-culture" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VI. After Constitutional Enshrinement: From Prohibition to Culture&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Article 1&#39;s constitutional enshrinement is not the end, but turning anti-predation from an external prohibition into Myriad Ranks&#39; inner culture. The Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, at every new cultivator&#39;s initiation rite, has them publicly confirm: every bit of energy they henceforth cultivate comes from creation and circulation, not from devouring others. This ritual looks formal, but actually nails a red line deep in consciousness — even if later reaching the highest realm, facing short-cut inner-demon temptation, this red line will still be awakened. The Alaya Network is responsible for external monitoring; this red line etched into initiation memory is responsible for inner self-discipline; internal and external joint force makes &quot;not using slaughter and predation as the evolutionary path&quot; truly become civilization&#39;s collective instinct.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><p><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: predated gains require enormous effort to refine and purify; Article 1&#39;s constitutional enshrinement eliminates this double waste at the source</p></li><li><p><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: this article is the anti-predation axiom itself, the whole charter&#39;s prohibition core</p></li><li><p><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang-Luo-type systems default the strong may take; Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s Article 1 directly negates &quot;the strong may take&quot; jurisprudence</p></li><li><p><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: the protected object is not some clan, but all possible predated ones, 99% coverage</p></li><li><p><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: the Great Dao&#39;s full-level openness is anti-predation&#39;s positive expression, opposing predatory private hoarding</p></li><li><p><strong>Universal equal infinity</strong>: every being inherently possesses basic infinite power; the easygoing layabouts retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will not be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes may superimpose higher-level infinity; predation thus fundamentally loses meaning</p></li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Article 1&#39;s constitutional enshrinement is the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization&#39;s total break with the old cosmic view. It tells Myriad Ranks: in Heng Yuan Zhou, the only legitimate way to evolve is to develop increments and co-build circulation; any attempt to walk the old road, from the moment the pen touches paper, is unconstitutional.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/04-反掠夺主义核心论纲.html">Entry 04 · Anti-Predationism Core Thesis</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/47-反垄断法.html">Entry 47 · Anti-Monopoly Law</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/19-修炼伦理与边界.html">Entry 19 · Cultivation Ethics and Boundaries</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/901_模块5-总论-文明终极定型法理基础.html">Entry 901 · Charter Overview</a></li><li>Official site: <a href="https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/</a></li></ul>',25)])])}const m=i(o,[["render",r]]);export{p as __pageData,m as default};
